+\begin{proposition}[Conditional recovery from noisy flow observations]\label{n:univup}
+Let $N,L\ge1$ and $0<\delta<1$. Let the observer record aggregate flow at $L$ fixed histories $h^{(1)},\ldots,h^{(L)}$ with independent Gaussian noise of variance $\sigma^2$ in each of $N$ experiments, and write $G(\nu)=(F_\nu(h^{(l)}))_{l\le L}$. Let $\mathcal K$ be a compact fixed-mass class with at most $K$ types and let $G$ be continuous, so a minimum exists. Suppose that on $\mathcal K$ the inverse bound $\|G(\nu)-G(\nu')\|\ge c_0\,W_1(\nu,\nu')^{2K-1}$ holds with $c_0>0$ independent of the spreads under comparison. Then the minimum-distance estimator $\hat\nu\in\arg\min_{\mu\in\mathcal K}\|G(\mu)-\bar y\|$ satisfies, with probability at least $1-\delta$,
 \[
 W_1(\hat\nu,\nu)\le\Big(\frac{2\sigma\big(\sqrt L+\sqrt{2\log(1/\delta)}\big)}{c_0\sqrt N}\Big)^{1/(2K-1)},
 \]
